From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "D.R.racer" <drracer@seznam.cz>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 19:34:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: separate the data direction from the
 stateful API

The driver has two nodes and infers everything from proc->role: the
stateless decoder has the bitstream on OUTPUT and uses requests, the
stateful encoder has it on CAPTURE and drains with LAST/EOS. A stateful
decoder (bitstream on OUTPUT, no requests) breaks that inference.

Keep role as the direction and add a stateful flag to the proc
configuration, together with the node name and request support:
- streaming state, drain, LAST on a CAPTURE buffer queued while
  stopped and the EOS subscription follow the stateful flag;
  requires_requests is set for stateless nodes only;
- DECODER_CMD dispatches to the stateful m2m helpers on a stateful
  decoder, the SOURCE_CHANGE event is offered there, and such a node
  keeps G_SELECTION;
- the watchdog names the node, and the spurious IRQ path walks all
  nodes;
- an engine flag, set for the H.264 encoder, asks for a VE reset after
  an error IRQ, replacing the encoder role test.

The VE reset that guarded decode jobs after encode jobs is now keyed on
the engine instead of the role, so it also runs when two engines of one
node alternate (e.g. H.264 and MPEG-2 decode), which share VE_MODE. The
last engine is cleared whenever the VE was reset (watchdog, error IRQ,
runtime resume), so the next job no longer resets a VE that was just
reset. These two are the only changes in behaviour for the existing
nodes.

Controls are no longer mandatory for a node.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
